We understand you have couple of options and would like to test which is most feasible for your use case, one of which is cloud functions. Based on our discussion,\'a0 I assume you will be triggering your cloud function via HTTP request. The custom role will grant you permissions needed to deploy cloud functions via gcloud CLI using your local credentials.\
\
Below is the sample shell script that I used to deploy cloud function for HTTP request.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \cb5 #!/bin/bash\
# Exit on error\
set -e\
\
# --- Configuration ---\
FUNCTION_NAME="test-gcs-nodejs-function"\
REGION="us-central1"\
RUNTIME="nodejs22"\
ENTRY_POINT="helloHttp" # The name of the function inside main.py\
# These should be passed as arguments or environment variables\
PROJECT_ID="dj-data-warehouse"\
SERVICE_ACCOUNT_NAME="adpt-credential-rotation-test"\
SA_EMAIL="$\{SERVICE_ACCOUNT_NAME\}@$\{PROJECT_ID\}.iam.gserviceaccount.com"\
\
\
echo "Deploying $\{FUNCTION_NAME\} to $\{PROJECT_ID\}..."\
\
gcloud functions deploy $\{FUNCTION_NAME\} \\\
  --gen2 \\\
  --project="$\{PROJECT_ID\}" \\\
  --region="$\{REGION\}" \\\
  --runtime="$\{RUNTIME\}" \\\
  --source=./function_code \\\
  --entry-point="$\{ENTRY_POINT\}" \\\
  --trigger-http \\\
  --run-service-account="$\{SA_EMAIL\}" \\\
  --no-allow-unauthenticated \\\
  --ingress-settings="all"\
\
gcloud functions add-invoker-policy-binding $\{FUNCTION_NAME\} \\\
  --member="user:aruna.morisetti@dowjones.com" \\\
  --region="$\{REGION\}" \\\
  --project="$\{PROJECT_ID\}"\
\
gcloud functions add-invoker-policy-binding $\{FUNCTION_NAME\} \\\
  --member="user:arun.mandal@dowjones.com" \\\
  --region="$\{REGION\}" \\\
  --project="$\{PROJECT_ID\}"\
\
echo "Deployment complete! Your function is now live."\cb1 \
